.TH DANBY-RUNNING 1
.SH NAME
danby-running \- coupled speed, fatigue, cadence, and distance model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/running
.SH MODEL
Forward acceleration is propulsive drive reduced by fatigue, minus a quadratic
resistance, divided by body mass.  Fatigue accumulates with speed squared and
recovers proportionally.  Stride length converts speed into gait phase.
.SH DISPLAY
The articulated runner is driven by the integrated gait phase.  The graph shows
speed and cumulative distance, so animation and quantitative state agree.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/running.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mechanism (2)
